      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the dimensions of Mateen's rectangular backyard and then calculate its area. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( l \\) meters and the width by \\( w \\) meters.\n\nFirst, we know from the problem statement that walking the length 25 times requires 1000 meters. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\\[\n25l = 1000\n\\]\nSolving for \\( l \\), we divide both sides by 25:\n\\[\nl = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nNext, we know that walking the perimeter 10 times also requires 1000 meters. Therefore, we can write the equation for the perimeter \\( P \\):\n\\[\nP = 2(l + w)\n\\]\nThe perimeter of the rectangle is also given by:\n\\[\nP = 2l + 2w\n\\]\nSince both expressions represent the perimeter, we can set them equal to each other:\n\\[\n2(l + w) = 1000\n\\]\nSubstituting the value of \\( l \\) that we found, \\( l = 40 \\), into the equation:\n\\[\n2(40 + w) = 1000\n\\]\nSimplifying inside the parentheses:\n\\[\n2(40 + w) = 1000\n\\]\nDividing both sides by 2:\n\\[\n40 + w = 500\n\\]\nSolving for \\( w \\):\n\\[\nw = 500 - 40 = 460 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the length and the width of the backyard, we can calculate the area \\( A \\) of the rectangle using the formula for the area of a rectangle:\n\\[\nA = l \\times w\n\\]\nSubstituting the values of \\( l \\) and \\( w \\):\n\\[\nA = 40 \\times 460 = 18400 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{18400}\\) square meters.",
