      "text": "To find the area of Mateen's backyard, we need to determine the dimensions of the rectangle first. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( L \\) meters and the width by \\( W \\) meters.\n\nAccording to the problem, Mateen can walk his backyard length 25 times to cover 1000 meters. This gives us the equation:\n\\[ 25L = 1000 \\]\nSolving for \\( L \\), we get:\n\\[ L = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNext, we know that Mateen can also walk the perimeter 10 times to cover 1000 meters. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[ P = 2L + 2W \\]\nSo, we have:\n\\[ 10P = 1000 \\]\nSolving for \\( P \\), we get:\n\\[ P = \\frac{1000}{10} = 100 \\text{ meters} \\]\nSubstituting the value of \\( L \\) into the perimeter equation, we get:\n\\[ 2(40) + 2W = 100 \\]\n\\[ 80 + 2W = 100 \\]\nSolving for \\( W \\), we get:\n\\[ 2W = 20 \\]\n\\[ W = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNow that we have the dimensions of the backyard, the area \\( A \\) is given by:\n\\[ A = L \\times W = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters} \\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\).",
