    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "1. **Understanding the problem**: \n   - We need to find the area of Mateen's rectangular backyard.\n   - We know that walking the length 25 times is equal to walking a kilometer (1000 meters).\n   - We also know that walking the perimeter 10 times is equal to walking a kilometer (1000 meters).\n\n2. **Setting up equations**:\n   - Let \\( l \\) be the length of the backyard and \\( w \\) be the width of the backyard.\n   - From the first piece of information, walking the length 25 times is equal to 1000 meters:\n     \\[\n     25l = 1000\n     \\]\n   - Solving for \\( l \\):\n     \\[\n     l = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters}\n     \\]\n\n   - From the second piece of information, walking the perimeter 10 times is equal to 1000 meters. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n     \\[\n     P = 2l + 2w\n     \\]\n   - Walking the perimeter 10 times is equivalent to 10 encounters, so:\n     \\[\n     10P = 1000\n     \\]\n   - Substituting \\( P = 2l + 2w \\) into the equation:\n     \\[\n     10(2l + 2w) = 1000\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying:\n     \\[\n     20l + 20w = 1000\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     l + w = 50\n     \\]\n\n3. **Solving for the width \\( w \\)**:\n   - Substitute \\( l = 40 \\) into the equation \\( l + w = 50 \\):\n     \\[\n     40 + w = 50\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     w = 50 - 40\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     w = 10 \\text{ meters}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Calculating the area**:\n   - The area \\( A \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n     \\[\n     A = l \\times w\n     \\]\n   - Substituting the values of \\( l \\) and \\( w \\):\n     \\[\n     A = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters}\n     \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\) square meters.",
